WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.840 line:10%
Lennart Meri
President of the Republic
speaking
on 24 February 1995:

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.520 line:10%
The open sea that carries
the Republic of Estonia

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.320 line:10%
is called international trust.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.560 line:10%
If the ship of state is shipshape,
it plows the waves

5
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.720
and moves towards our common goal,
which is hidden behind the horizon.

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.440
But if the ship of state is damaged,

7
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.640
if international trust fails
to keep the ship of state afloat,

8
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.400
we cannot reach our common goal.

9
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.760
We have to read the map,
use the chronometer and compass,

10
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.600
check the weather, know the winds,
currents and hidden rocks,

11
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.840
the capacity and speed of the engine.

12
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.200
We must also understand
the laconic international language

13
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:57.720
of other ships of state that we meet,
that overtake us or intersect our course.

14
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.400
Most importantly, the people
of Estonia and all other peoples

15
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.280
must know that on our bridge
work goes on 24/7

16
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.040
and nobody disappears
to the bar for the weekend.

17
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.400
It is only on such conditions
that the Estonian people

18
00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.840
can trust their state
and call it their own.

19
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.880
We shall tell you a story
about our native land Estonia.

20
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.760
The characters are our own people
with very different world-views.

21
00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.200
They board the ship and sail
for weeks around the Mediterranean.

22
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.000
People with conflicting world-views have
to manage on just a few square metres.

23
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.960
Paradoxically,
they all have to pull one rope

24
00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.920
in order to speed on with all sails set.

25
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.600
I really like storms.

26
00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.680
We wouldn’t want too many Muslims
to come to Europe and Estonia.

27
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.600
I’ve been a Muslim for some 14 years.

28
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.560
The only way to survive
in stormy waters

29
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.880
is to learn to know each other as
best as possible and work as a team.

30
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.440
Thus, the seamen will be tested
both physically and psychologically.

31
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.040
The crew is made up of:
Steven, a Muslim:

32
00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.040
People have to show tolerance
towards intolerance.

33
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.800
We have to stand up for
other minorities as well.

34
00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:38.280
Sanna, a feminist: I think it is
fertile soil for feminists to cultivate.

35
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:43.040
Knut Thor, a radical nationalist:
A Russian is a broad concept.

36
00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.680
I have nothing against a Russian

37
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.200
who thinks 20 August is
more important than 9 May,

38
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.160
who is ready to learn Estonian,
and work for Estonia.

39
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.760
Oleg, a Russian from Sillamäe:

40
00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:03.280
Sooner or later nationalism will stoke
up new fires in Auschwitz ovens.

41
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.640
Joosep, a gay man:

42
00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:11.360
Feminism, same-sex and opposite-sex
marriages, what's the difference?

43
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.640
Mati, a patriot interested in history,
from Viljandi:

44
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.400
Same-sex couples do not
produce children,

45
00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.320
but by the laws of nature,
there should be offspring.

46
00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.400
Riccardo, a seasoned seaman from Italy

47
00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.680
keeps an eye on this
unpredictable company.

48
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.600
First impressions are quite positive.

49
00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.520
The Viking seems to be
an interesting character,

50
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.480
though he sometimes makes
inappropriate, misogynistic jokes.

51
00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.680
Someone will kick up stink,
that’s for sure!

52
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.160
People have been leaving
their stuff around

53
00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.720
and we are going to have
a problem with trash.

54
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.880
We had some wine
with Joosep yesterday,

55
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.720
and then he was somewhat
different than today, when he is sober.

56
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.960
But he seems to be a cool guy.

57
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.680
Knut is a baby, to tell you the truth.

58
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.960
He is a child and I think
I have a lot to teach him.

59
00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.560
I have been talking mostly with Oleg.

60
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.080
We are not on the same
wavelength in all matters,

61
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.240
but it is interesting
to listen to different views;

62
00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.360
good to practice my Russian.

63
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.920
He’s also interested in history,
engages in interesting things,

64
00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.200
is member of the Sillamäe
municipal council.

65
00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.600
We discussed history, politics.

66
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.440
Very interesting.

67
00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.760
I’m sure we’ll have things to do,
once we set sail.

68
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.760
A seaman is a good man.

69
00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.680
Oleg
#Russian

70
00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.960
Fresh fish - good fish.

71
00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.040
Sanna
#Feminist

72
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.680
Salt spoils no fish.

73
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.640
Water for fish, air for birds,
all land for man.

74
00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.920
Steven
#Muslim

75
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.160
Cheap fish, watery soup.

76
00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.360
The bigger the fish,
the thicker the broth.

77
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.960
Mati
#Estonian guy

78
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.320
More fish make better soup.

79
00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.520
Better catch from muddy waters.

80
00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.200
Joosep
#LGBT

81
00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.560
A thousand nets,
a hundred fish.

82
00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.000
A fish never lives on dry land.

83
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.760
Knut Thor
#Nationalist

84
00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.520
Everyone is right:
landman and seaman.

85
00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.000
We will throw them …

86
00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.680
OVERBOARD

87
00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.600
Episode 1

88
00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.840
So, release,
release this rope!

89
00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.440
No-no, wait-wait!
Here we go!

90
00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.120
Good morning, this is the boat Tetina.

91
00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.440
We are leaving the harbour.

92
00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:29.560
OK, you are in a good position,
now you are the chief mate. - Yes!

93
00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:37.960
I think I will have no problems
controlling and leading my team.

94
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.880
At present I am trying to steer
the boat to the next destination.

95
00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.480
I have to keep an eye on the left side
of the island over there,

96
00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.560
and steer the boat there.

97
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.800
We are quite many here
and it could a problem

98
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.200
finding something
for everyone to do.

99
00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:01.600
At present there’s a lot of sitting
around, smoking, having nothing to do,

100
00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:05.880
but I am sure that under my gentle
leadership we’ll soon have tasks for all.

101
00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:09.440
I am standing by the sail,
waiting for orders.

102
00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.440
Life is hard.

103
00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:16.640
People learn to know each other and
each other’s problems. This is cool.

104
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.760
The sails are set.
Now is the time to ask,

105
00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.440
what the crew members think of
each other’s views and opinions.

106
00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.600
Attitudes about right-wing radicals -

107
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.040
I think they are lacking a bit in
education and have too many fears.

108
00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.960
Actually, Islam is not a religion of
peace, according to the Quran.

109
00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.720
Stop now. I don’t want to have
anything to do with them.

110
00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:45.080
I don’t want to listen
to what they are saying.

111
00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:51.000
To the best of my knowledge, my fellow
voyagers have different views of life.

112
00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.400
I think it is difficult to grow up
as a Russian in Estonia.

113
00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:03.040
I am indifferent towards
feminism as a movement,

114
00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:08.480
because I don’t see any
serious problems there.

115
00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.320
He does not even speak
the official language,

116
00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.800
but is employed by the state and lives
here - this is unacceptable for me.

117
00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:21.200
The person does not even
understand that they cause a lot of pain

118
00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.760
to a group or groups of
people with their words.

119
00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:27.720
History has shown that
too much liberalism

120
00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.400
can even lead to
the perishing of civilisations.

121
00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.560
Pirates of the Caribbean!

122
00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:43.360
2000 years old!
- I am Jack Sparrow.

123
00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.600
You - no way!
- Yes, look at my hair!

124
00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.680
OK, then I am Orlando Bloom,
he was also in this film.

125
00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.200
Dolphins!
- Really?

126
00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.520
Everything starts happening
at the same time!

127
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:57.880
What’s going on?

128
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.240
Good Lord, yes, they are playing around!
- They are pulling our leg!

129
00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.960
No! Where are they?
- Up front!

130
00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:10.200
Why you can see them and I can’t?
There’s a whole lot of them!

131
00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.360
The first day at sea has passed.

132
00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.280
The crew members are poking
each other for attitudes and opinions.

133
00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.600
There’ve been some
heart-to-heart talks.

134
00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.160
But some have had their pain
threshold tested as well.

135
00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.920
It was back in the 1990s
or even 1980s,

136
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.720
when every stranger
was punched in the face

137
00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.120
as soon as he arrived,
no questions asked.

138
00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.280
Those were the times,
but they are no more.

139
00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:00.400
All my life I have walked with my
eyes in the back of my head.

140
00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:04.920
Sometimes I am scared to death
to walk on the streets.

141
00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:11.920
I get shouted at five to ten times every
day, both in Estonian and in Russian.

142
00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:16.080
I worry madly whether
I make it home in the evenings.

143
00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:22.800
Not every night, but fairly often.
Most of the time I just accept it,

144
00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:27.360
for this is my daily
cross to bear.

145
00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.880
But then sometimes,
when I am tired,

146
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:37.160
I think, why do I have to have
eyes in the back of my head.

147
00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.680
It makes me hysterical,
wanting to cry,

148
00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:45.520
to escape, lock myself up at home,
for I do not dare step outside.

149
00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:48.520
This is not OK.
Do I approve of Gay Pride?

150
00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.000
I do not like it because
of the way it is organised.

151
00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.680
It should be a bit more dignified.

152
00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.280
We do not want to show that
all gays are some kind of weirdos.

153
00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:03.720
I would rather want to show that
there are normal people as well.

154
00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.440
Did you go this year?
- No, I did not.

155
00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:10.240
It was very decent.
- Yes, that’s what I heard as well.

156
00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:14.200
You do not have to march there with
bare boobs and feathers up your arse.

157
00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:18.560
In my opinion this smears
the good name of gays.

158
00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.680
Let me say this, and be done
with it once and for all:

159
00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:26.560
as I told you earlier today, I think
it all comes down to the media.

160
00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:31.400
But listening to you today…
you are a person

161
00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.400
who made me look at all this
from an entirely different angle.

162
00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.680
Your talents and what you are.

163
00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.080
I think we have managed with
the Russians quite well.

164
00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.760
We have been entirely open
and I hope that the Russians

165
00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.600
want to integrate into our society.

166
00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.480
Although, it could have gone better.

167
00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.040
Oleg, for example,
should speak Estonian.

168
00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.240
He’s been raised here,
so why doesn’t he?

169
00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.160
Why can’t he speak Estonian?

170
00:11:56.280 --> 00:12:00.200
Well, the thing is, that when
I went to school in Sillamäe,

171
00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:06.760
we never had Estonian language
as one of the subjects.

172
00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.160
I was carefully listening
to you and I have a question,

173
00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:16.720
which does not require
a long answer.

174
00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:28.320
In your opinion, is Estonia only
your country or is it mine too?

175
00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:35.600
We must not stoke up tensions
and turn some groups against others.

176
00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:42.160
Not on any grounds - ethnic,
national, language or social ones.

177
00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.400
After all, there is the law on equal
rights and the Estonian constitution.

178
00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:52.720
I do not understand why people
whose job is to make sure

179
00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:54.840
that everyone abides by the law,

180
00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:59.400
do not sanction those
who say things like that.

181
00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.600
I would really like to ask
people who are saying

182
00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:08.400
that Russians are a cancerous
growth on the body of Estonia,

183
00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:15.560
what on earth do you want? Civil war?
Massacre? We’ve had all this already.

184
00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:21.160
First of all, such discussions
help us understand each other.

185
00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:26.840
It’s not important
if it’s heated or not.

186
00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:31.240
Views can be different,
even conflicting.

187
00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:37.920
But even so, it is necessary
to come to some agreement,

188
00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.880
find a common language.

189
00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.840
Or at least understand
the views of others,

190
00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.640
even if you are not able
to accept them.

191
00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:49.400
Yesterday there were
two moments for me.

192
00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.360
Our Joosep.

193
00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:03.720
There has been kind of a change in me.
When I first saw him at the airport,

194
00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:10.040
I had a problem accepting him,
I thought he was showing off.

195
00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.960
And later I realised
how cool a guy he is.

196
00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:19.400
And along with getting
to know a homosexual -

197
00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:23.320
I do not know, if he is one.
- Yes, he is.

198
00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:28.280
So, I do not think any more …
or I came to understand that…

199
00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:32.720
Well, think what the media
has been saying about

200
00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:36.720
this group of people …
but I have a different view now,

201
00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:40.440
because I have gotten myself
a good acquaintance,

202
00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:43.360
if not yet a friend as one of them.

203
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:48.160
Given that he is so cool, the others
cannot be that much worse.

204
00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:53.160
Actually, we have been able
to talk normally with even Mati.

205
00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.560
But our Viking scared
me a bit yesterday,

206
00:14:55.680 --> 00:15:00.000
when he tried to stop me
interfering by using his hands.

207
00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.800
After his hand touched my face,

208
00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.600
I wasn’t so keen on
saying anything further.

209
00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:12.400
Actually, we could not finish the topic,
I guess we continue today.

210
00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:18.360
We arrive at the Port of Epidaurus.

211
00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:22.160
This tiny town has the oldest
amphitheatre in Greece,

212
00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:26.280
admired for its exceptional acoustics.
There are also lots of cats.

213
00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:31.320
Comedy, tragedy, as well as drama
were performed here in ancient times.

214
00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:36.920
From an asshole to assholes.
- I am not a homosexual!

215
00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:44.120
Age means nothing when it comes
to wisdom or the ability to argue.

216
00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:47.800
You can’t tell me what pitch
I can use when talking!

217
00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:49.640
Yes, I can!

218
00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.800
We could keep and feed
OUR OWN, white people,

219
00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:56.920
and not gather all sorts
of potential criminals,

220
00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.000
Muslims, negroes, parasites
from all over the world!

221
00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.400
Often the performances
were dedicated to Dionysus,

222
00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:07.160
and they could turn out to be
orgies lasting for days,

223
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.960
serving as a hint of
what was to come.

224
00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:14.160
I think people are born good.

225
00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:20.920
In ancient Greece plays were
based on words and speaking.

226
00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:26.200
The actors wore masks, which
depicted the nature, gender, age

227
00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:29.040
and social status of the characters.

228
00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:34.760
Will our characters maintain or lose
their masks - we’ll see as we go along.

229
00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:50.400
Well, dear countrymen,
we have come to a point now,

230
00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.240
where each of us has
to step on this stone here

231
00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:58.680
and explain in short and clear terms,
what will your future Estonia be like.

232
00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:04.120
Joosep
#Gay

233
00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.440
I think that in my future Estonia

234
00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.440
all sorts of backward thinking
pensioners and old-timers

235
00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:11.840
should pull themselves
together and admit

236
00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.120
that it was them, who left all this
shit to the current generations;

237
00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:18.120
they should also come
to grips with the idea

238
00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:21.680
that it is the 21st century,
the world is open,

239
00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.160
the borders are open, please
move along with the times,

240
00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:28.120
you cannot expect young
people marching to your beat,

241
00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:31.040
because you are old!

242
00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:33.880
Yuck! Rubbish!

243
00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:35.600
Knut Thor
#Nationalist

244
00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:40.240
In my future Estonia people
have a greater say in state matters.

245
00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:44.760
And there is more understanding
between people and politicians.

246
00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.480
Steven
#Muslim

247
00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.680
I have heard that at the time
when Al-Qaeda

248
00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:57.640
was mainly in control in Afghanistan,
there were guys with little sticks

249
00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:04.920
checking the pubes of men in the street,
for the hair should not be too long.

250
00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.800
This habit has
disappeared apparently.

251
00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:17.080
There are similar guys
with sticks in Estonia too,

252
00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:20.080
they want to check
all sorts of things.

253
00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.240
In my Estonia we should
have very few of such guys

254
00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:26.840
or better still, none whatsoever.

255
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.480
Oleg
#Russian

256
00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:33.280
We must do everything
to avoid conflicts in the society.

257
00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:36.000
For it to develop socially.

258
00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:41.280
So that we could come to agreement
even if we have different interests

259
00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:44.000
and speak different languages.

260
00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:49.920
Estonia has to be home for all,
not just for a chosen few.

261
00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:53.240
And most important:

262
00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:59.200
Estonia must restore her independence!
At present Estonia is not independent!

263
00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.200
Mati
#Estonian guy

264
00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:05.040
My future Estonia:
There are no political parties,

265
00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.160
there is no president.

266
00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:09.800
We have participatory
democracy, direct democracy,

267
00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.080
knowledge-based society, openness.

268
00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:14.560
Sanna
#Feminist

269
00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:18.240
Why is crying, and expressing deep and
difficult emotions actually good for you?

270
00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:21.040
I have a girlfriend who told me

271
00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:24.640
that once she could not
go to the loo for 8 days.

272
00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:29.640
She was badly constipated,
so she really could not go for 8 days.

273
00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:34.200
What happens to a person,
when all this remains inside?

274
00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.240
It poisons the insides.

275
00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:41.080
When we use the same logic for tears,
emotions kept inside turn sour as well

276
00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:47.160
and may finally emerge as anger.

277
00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:51.440
In other words - let’s give
people back their tears!

278
00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:54.720
Old people are not able
to keep up with the pace,

279
00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:58.120
but they are unwilling
to give up their position

280
00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:02.480
or admit that they are
no longer competent.

281
00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:06.560
If you have been doing
something for 20 years,

282
00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.920
it means that you should have
given it up already 15 years ago.

283
00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:19.640
Joosep, the most colourful person of the
lot attacked the elderly for what they are,

284
00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:24.960
even if just before that we were
speaking about understanding each other

285
00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:27.880
and allowing everyone
come out of the closet.

286
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.680
Joosep does not like the thoughts
and words of old people,

287
00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:34.000
Joosep expects the elderly
to accept him,

288
00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.840
so why doesn’t he accept them?

289
00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:42.880
My name is Joosep and I am
what you call a multitasker.

290
00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:50.360
Being any kind of radical is
not necessary in my opinion.

291
00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:56.920
Given that I am a bit of
a choleric myself,

292
00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:01.760
I’m afraid that I may
get angry with someone

293
00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:04.680
and say things without
thinking first.

294
00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:08.360
But I believe that I am
able to control myself.

295
00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:12.640
I think it is necessary and
very welcome indeed,

296
00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:17.160
if a real discussion emerges
between the very different persons,

297
00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:20.640
without anyone getting angry.

298
00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:24.240
I hope we will be able to do so.

299
00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:29.200
It is the evening in Epidaurus.

300
00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.440
To the astonishment of the crew,

301
00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:34.960
Mati is made the new chief mate
of the Tetina.

302
00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.920
You are in charge now.

303
00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.400
You think you can manage
to control the team?

304
00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.840
Thank you.
- Good luck!

305
00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:48.840
Winston Churchill, when he became
Britain’s prime minister during WWII,

306
00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:53.480
said that all his past life had been
but a preparation for that hour and trial.

307
00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:56.520
I too can say that
all my prior experience

308
00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:59.720
and the few days that
I have spent with these people

309
00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:04.680
with whom I have to start working,
allow me to say that I will manage all right.

310
00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:09.840
I have led groups to victory in cases
which were considered impossible.

311
00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:13.440
And those groups
have been bigger by far.

312
00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:19.680
Having seen Steven
offer to do the dishes

313
00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:24.800
and Oleg cut the potatoes
and all others act in the same manner -

314
00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:29.040
giving a hand whenever they can.

315
00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:39.680
The youngest among us, when he
was first offered to take over the rudder,

316
00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:41.640
asked, who was to be responsible.

317
00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:45.640
But as soon as he stood there,
his face was full of enthusiasm

318
00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:49.880
and he managed very well
when we had to change the sail.

319
00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:53.920
You feel like a captain and
the crew does all the work

320
00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:56.120
and you just turn the rudder.

321
00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:00.920
I can be considered a conservative.

322
00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:03.800
You cannot go against
the laws of nature.

323
00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:05.880
Being a patriot means
you are rich.

324
00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:07.800
There is diversity
in nature as well,

325
00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:09.720
and there are dickheads
among every nation.

326
00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.200
Now well, here we go.

327
00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:37.960
First, the girl here was
chief mate, now it’s me.

328
00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:43.760
I was told that I have
to be in charge for three days.

329
00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:49.120
We must be ready
to be at sea for 28 hours.

330
00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:53.440
This means that tonight
as the first thing

331
00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:56.600
we have to work out the
watchkeeping schedule.

332
00:23:56.720 --> 00:23:59.400
For that we make up pairs -
as equal as possible:

333
00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:05.280
Oleg and Joosep, Knut and Steven,
and I and our crew member

334
00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:11.240
sporting a crew cut - Sanna.

335
00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:15.120
The weather forecast
does not look promising.

336
00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:18.280
It is going to be
a stormy night at sea.

337
00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:22.760
Watch teams have been determined
and everyone must follow the orders

338
00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:24.640
of the new chief mate Mati.

339
00:24:24.760 --> 00:24:27.080
Nobody opposes.

340
00:24:27.560 --> 00:24:30.800
Isn’t it so that at the beginning
everybody hopes for the best.

341
00:24:30.920 --> 00:24:33.600
The decision has been made,
all lines are clear

342
00:24:33.720 --> 00:24:37.680
and the boat heads to
the Mediterranean in total darkness.

343
00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:40.920 line:10%
Lennart Meri
President of the Republic:

344
00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:43.720 line:10%
Estonia has never been
a great nation in power,

345
00:24:44.120 --> 00:24:46.600 line:10%
but we have been and can again
become a great nation in spirit,

346
00:24:46.760 --> 00:24:48.720 line:10%
by being ourselves.

347
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:54.560
It is possible to be ourselves
only in an open society,

348
00:24:55.640 --> 00:24:58.240
not by resorting to ring-fencing.

349
00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:00.600
Everyone feels euphoric,

350
00:25:00.720 --> 00:25:04.360
despite having to get
ready for the rough sea.

351
00:25:05.040 --> 00:25:07.880
High winds and
storms are forecast.

352
00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:10.760
The winds are roaring,

353
00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:13.840
mighty waves are crashing
against the hull.

354
00:25:13.920 --> 00:25:18.920
Inevitably the tempestuous weather
is reflected in the crew as well.

355
00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:24.280
The winds had not died
down by the morning

356
00:25:24.520 --> 00:25:28.920
and captain Riccardo
has to take over.

357
00:25:30.720 --> 00:25:33.160
The storm is getting worse.

358
00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:51.400
It is even difficult for such seasoned
seaman as the captain to keep the course.

359
00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:55.120
Had the inexperienced crew
been left alone in this weather,

360
00:25:55.200 --> 00:25:57.720
the yacht could have easily sunk.

361
00:25:58.320 --> 00:26:00.960
Will the relations among
the crew be as stormy -

362
00:26:01.080 --> 00:26:04.520
we’ll learn in the next
episode, in a week’s time.

363
00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:06.360
What is really wrong with Estonia?

364
00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:07.920
What can be done?

365
00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:10.280
Why is Mati behaving like that?

366
00:26:10.360 --> 00:26:12.520
Why is he communicating
with the world around him

367
00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:16.040
in such an intense and
incomprehensible manner?

368
00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:20.320
Bullshit!
Shut up, negro!

369
00:26:20.880 --> 00:26:22.440
Stop!

370
00:26:22.920 --> 00:26:25.680
In Paris the problem
is that non-whites,

371
00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:30.640
all sorts of blacks and people from
the Middle East urinate on the streets.

372
00:26:30.720 --> 00:26:33.280
The nationalistic
end is slightly racist

373
00:26:33.440 --> 00:26:37.480
and the conservative end
is more homophobic.

374
00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:42.720
This clearly shows their way
of thinking, nothing else.

375
00:26:43.640 --> 00:26:45.200
The Immortal Regiment!

376
00:26:45.280 --> 00:26:47.600
The Internal Security Service
clearly has to keep an eye

377
00:26:47.680 --> 00:26:49.920
on the Immortal Regiment,
just in case.

378
00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:51.640
Listen, young people,
you are just daft,

379
00:26:51.760 --> 00:26:54.840
you have absolutely
no clue about life, you are …

380
00:26:54.960 --> 00:26:58.160
Are you asking for
a smack on your face?

381
